This explicit `gui_host=chimera` scaffold imports the maintained public Go host
`github.com/hollis-labs/chimera {{ .inputs.chimera_version }}`. Folio renders thin
wiring; there is no copied host implementation, replace directive or go.work.
The original frontend and app-owned API remain in this project.

## Reproducible dependencies

- Go {{ .inputs.go_version }} (the canonical portfolio floor).
- Node 22.12+ and npm, compatible with the pinned Vite 7.3.6.
- `chimera_gui_recipe={{ .inputs.chimera_gui_recipe }}`: published design packages 0.4.0,
  React/ReactDOM 19.3.0 and the exact committed frontend lock/integrities.
- The shared runtime/build lock entries are the reviewed Chimera389 closure;
  the Folio starter adds its existing published kit and lint-tool dependencies.
  Both root lock names are templated with the project name.

`design_kit_version` and `go_webui_version` configure only the legacy `go-webui`
branch. This branch uses the explicit fixed enum pins above, also recorded in
`.folio.yaml` and `chimera-provenance.json`. An upgrade is a separately reviewed
preset change with a new compatible lock, never a silent npm resolution.

## Explicit build and run

```sh
cd frontend
npm ci
npm run typecheck
npm run lint
npm run build
cd ..
go mod tidy
go test ./...
go build -o {{ .inputs.project_name }} ./cmd/{{ .inputs.project_name }}
./{{ .inputs.project_name }}
```

Folio itself performs none of these install/build/run operations. The frontend
build writes into `internal/webui/dist`; the server embeds those bytes and
imports Chimera directly. Full MIT terms are in `licenses/Chimera-MIT.txt`.

GUI base: `{{ .inputs.base_path }}`. Browser URL:
<http://127.0.0.1:8080{{ trimSuffix "/" .inputs.base_path }}/>. Root `/` stays `/`,
not `//`. Deep local routes reload through the same embedded SPA; assets use
that canonical base. Reserved host bases `/api`, `/plugins` and `/healthz` are
refused by Chimera. APIs remain at root `/api/health` and the bounded 64 KiB local `/api/messages` echo.
The echo is a local demonstration, not a provider/agent transport.

`LISTEN_ADDR` defaults to loopback 127.0.0.1:8080. Override it explicitly if needed;
update Vite's API proxy if changing the development port. `make ui-dev` runs
Vite separately, proxying the app's root `/api`. Ctrl+C/SIGTERM drains the
maintained HTTP host. Missing `/api` routes return 404 rather than SPA content.

The renderer preserves atomic materialization, LF-normalized breadcrumb file
digests and read-only `folio inspect` drift reporting. `folio sync` remains an
erroring stub. No publication, install/enable, persistence or business policy is
provided by this shell recipe.
