A chat-first React app on published design-kit and `kit-chat`, served by a Go
binary through `go-webui`. Scaffolded by `folio new chat-app`.

## Layout

```text
cmd/{{ .inputs.project_name }}/   Go server: /api/health and /api/messages
internal/webui/                 embedded frontend build + go-webui handler
frontend/src/App.tsx            AppShell, conversation sidebar, header
frontend/src/pages/chat.tsx     host-owned draft/transcript + ChatStream/ChatInput
frontend/src/api/               same-origin runtime client and typed context
```

`ChatStream` fills the remaining height above a bordered `ChatInput`, following
ops-chat's composition. The app owns draft, messages, request state and reset.
The starter `/api/messages` endpoint returns a local echo; it has no agent-service
dependency, credentials, streaming transport or persistent conversation storage.
Replace that endpoint/client with your own transport. "New conversation" resets
the current local transcript.

## Develop and build

Requires Go {{ .inputs.go_version }}+ and Node.js 20+ / npm.

```sh
make run       # Go server on 127.0.0.1:8080
make ui-dev    # Vite, proxying /api to the Go server
make all       # build frontend, then the single embedded Go binary
```

Use the Vite URL during development; the Go binary serves the built app at
<http://localhost:8080{{ .inputs.base_path }}/>. Before the first frontend build,
`go-webui` serves its "not built" placeholder. The Go listener defaults to
`127.0.0.1:8080`. For containers, set `LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8080` explicitly to
listen on all interfaces. Set `LISTEN_ADDR` to choose another address or port;
if changing the development port, update Vite's API proxy to match.

## Styling and package versions

`design_kit_version={{ .inputs.design_kit_version }}` supplies the published
foundation, kit-chat and design ESLint package versions. The default is
**0.4.0**, generating `^0.4.0` ranges for the published 0.4.x packages. This
release retains the 13px bubble/composer typography and built-in Send
control, with its small Button now using the 6px control radius. The starter
delegates sending to `ChatInput` rather than adding a second control. Override the input deliberately when choosing another version;
existing generated apps are not updated automatically.

The CSS imports Tailwind v4, the token theme, base component source registration,
**kit-chat/source.css**, and the runtime shell reset. Keep the kit-chat source
import: Tailwind does not scan package class strings automatically, and a green
build can still render an unstyled transcript. The starter selects token theme
`dir-a` in dark mode. It uses plain message content; the optional markdown lane
and streamdown are not installed.

The TypeScript config allows `.ts` import extensions under `noEmit`, as required
by the published design-bindings source reached through kit-chat.

Runtime transport comes from `design-app-runtime`, AppShell/base controls from
`design-components`, and transcript/composer from `kit-chat`. App code names
contract tokens rather than raw color or scale values.

## Checks

```sh
cd frontend
npm install
npm run typecheck
npm run lint    # Biome + the design-token ESLint config
npm run build
```

Generated CI runs these checks before Go vet/build/test so the server embeds a
real UI. `make test` and `make vet` check the Go app. See Folio's opt-in consumer
verification for a real headless-browser check of emitted styles and message send.

